        "note_tweet": {
          "text": "Sharing my pstack NSWF prompt. Your repo will never be the same...in a good way of course:\n\nUse /poteto-mode on this repo. First, find the mistakes agents and humans keep repeating here: read the git log, past bug fixes and review comments. Then make each one impossible instead of documenting it. Try architecture first, then types, then a lint whose error names the fix, then a test. Delete comments that restate code, and encode the constraint behind any comment that matters (/no-comments). Where concurrency, retries or state machines cause real bugs, write a formal model that replays a past bug and fails on it (/create-formal-verification-skill), and run it in CI. Replace unit tests that pin implementation with those models plus real DB and e2e tests, but keep every test that guards security or legal behavior. Ship one verifiable PR per step, and prove each check catches a real past mistake before you trust it."
        },
